            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0816" n="808" xml:id="pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/849: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-26T19:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>655. [For Rublee.] Your 1245, October 26, 4 p.m. Your letter is approved. With
                    respect to your second observation, we suggest that the procedure in
                    ascertaining the numbers and types of Sudetens who must emigrate and in
                    ascertaining possible opportunities for settlement be coordinated as closely as
                    possible with that followed concerning the involuntary emigrants already coming
                    within the Committee’s competence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
